forks":1606,"open_issues":205,"watchers":11252,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"[I'm afraid I can't email from my work machine on which I'm encountering this issue, so can't send a full stack trace, or reproducible code.]\r\nUsing Python 3.9.4 on linux, my program runs fine using SQLAlchemy versions <=1.4.15, but with versions >=1.4.16 I get the following error message:\r\n```\r\nsqlalchemy.exc.DBAPIError: (pyodbc.Error) ('01000', \"[01000] [unixODBC][Driver Manager]Can't open lib 'ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server?autocommit=True' : file not found (0) (SQLDriverConnect)\")\r\n```\r\nNothing else changes other than the SQLAlchemy version (installed via `conda install sqlalchemy=1.4.xx`).\r\nThe connection url is of the form `'mssql+pyodbc://@HOST/DATABASE?driver=ODBC+Driver+17+for+SQL+Server?autocommit=True'`.\r\n\r\nThe error occurs in `MetaData.reflect()`:\r\n```\r\nmetadata = sa.MetaData()\r\nmetadata.reflect(engine, schema=schema, only=only)\r\n```\r\n\r\nSorry for not being able to provide more details, but I'm happy to answer any questions and test proposed changes.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6601/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6601/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]